  "description": "Variation of condition 1 (approved plans) attached to planning permission 2020/3363 dated 09/04/2021 for 'Demolition of existing single storey garages at the rear of 141 Evering Road\r\n(otherwise known as 19 Maury Road) and the erection of a 3 bed, three storey single\r\nfamily dwellinghouse.'The effect of the variation would be to amend the roof form, amend window locations, remove the rear lightwell and relocate the bike and bin store.&nbsp;",
  "lapsed_date": null,
  "lpa_app_no": "2022/0365",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:16:02.457Z",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "site_name": null,
  "appeal_decision_date": null,
  "site_number": "141",
  "appeal_decision": null,
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;\tNotwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning General Development Order 1988 (or any Order revoking and re-enacting that Order), planning permission shall be required in respect of development falling within Classes A- G of Part 1 of the second schedule to that Order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect the character and appearance of the development hereby approved.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with 09/04/2021.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development hereby approved shall be designed and constructed to meet water efficiency requirements with a maximum internal water use of 105 litres/person/day, plus an allowance of 5 litres/person/day for external water use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure the development contributes to minimising the need for further water infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the first occupation of the development,&amp;nbsp; the on site bicycle storage facilities for 2no. bicycles, shown on the plans hereby approved, shall be installed prior to the first occupation of the development and shall thereafter be retained and maintained.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure that adequate provision for the safe and secure storage of bicycles is made for future occupiers and in the interest of safeguarding highway safety.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby approved a minimum of one bat box shall be provided at or close to eaves level of the development hereby approved. The box(es) shall be retained thereafter in perpetuity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: In the interests of enhancing and promoting biodiversity within the Borough&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the first occupation of the development,&amp;nbsp; the on site refuse and recycling storage, shown on the plans hereby approved, shall be installed prior to the first occupation of the development and shall thereafter be retained and maintained.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure that adequate provision for the storage of refuse and recycling is made for future occupiers and in the interest of safeguarding highway safety.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;\tNotwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning General Development Order 1988 (or any Order revoking and re-enacting that Order), no additional windows or doors shall be placed in either the northern or southern elevations of the building, hereby approved.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect the residential amenity of neighbouring properties.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Detailed drawings/full particulars of the proposed development showing the matters set out below must be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority, in writing, before the relevant work is commenced. The development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the details thus approved which shall be implemented in full prior to the first occupation/use of the development and retained in perpetuity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;a) Privacy screen on the southern edge of the first floor terrace&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: In the interests of protecting the amenity of neighbouring residential properties.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;All non-Combined Heat and Power space and hot water fossil fuel (or equivalent hydrocarbon based fuel) boilers must achieve dry NOx emission levels equivalent to or less than 40 mg/kWh.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect air quality and human health by ensuring that the production of air pollutants are kept to a minimum during the course of building works and during the lifetime of the development.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
